This is a small REST-style HTTP server in C (POSIX sockets, a custom bounded
thread pool, SQLite). It is network-facing C: correctness, memory safety, and
clear invariants outrank feature velocity. The authoritative guide is
[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) — read it for architecture and full commands.

## Build & check commands
- Build: `make` (or `make strict` for `-Werror`).
- Format: `make format-check` / `make format` (clang-format, `.clang-format`).
- Static analysis: `make cppcheck`.
- Parser unit + fuzz (ASan/UBSan): `make http-test`.
- Runtime memory check: `make valgrind`.
- Tests: `cd tests && pytest -v` (the suite builds/manages its own server).
- All of the above must pass before a PR; CI runs the same stages.

## Module boundaries (put code where the concern lives)
- `src/server.c` — sockets, accept loop, IP allowlist, `route_request`.
- `src/http.c` — request framing + parsing (the parsers do no socket I/O).
- `src/response.c` — HTTP response construction.
- `src/views.c` — endpoint handlers; map DB results to HTTP status.
- `src/database.c` — SQLite CRUD (prepared statements) + bounded JSON.
- `src/threadpool.c` — bounded worker pool.
- `include/models.h` — the compile-time data model (edit this to change schema).

## Invariants — do not regress (see AGENTS.md for the full list)
- Requests are framed via `recv_request` (Content-Length aware); never treat one
  `recv` as a whole request.
- Route on parsed `(method, target)`, never `strstr` over raw bytes.
- All SQL values go through `sqlite3_bind_*`; never concatenate input into SQL.
- JSON is built with the bounded, escaping `strbuf` builder; fail closed (`500`)
  on overflow.
- DB writers hold `db_write_lock` across `step()` + `sqlite3_changes()`.
- The `SIGINT` handler only sets a `sig_atomic_t`; cleanup runs in normal context.
- A malformed request or DB error fails that request (correct status), never
  `exit()`s the process.
- Every fixed buffer is bounded (`snprintf`/bounded loops); no
  `strcpy`/`strcat`/`sprintf`/unbounded scans.
- Keep `NUM_COLS` equal to the number of `TABLE_COLS` rows (`_Static_assert`).

## Style
- C, Allman braces, 4-space indent (run `make format`). Keep the tree clean
  under `-Werror`, ASan/UBSan, and Valgrind. Keep comments truthful — a
  misleading comment is treated as a bug.

